ed  resume  rather than a timeline empathy has  taught me that people need to really  quickly understand if they should call a  candidate up or not within the first 30  seconds of reviewing a resume  so really save your detailed experiences  for interviews and  only share a few relevant items that  make employers curious to learn more  about you  my one tip for women in tech just don't  be afraid of trying different  technologies and  roles you might surprise yourself with  what you find and what you like  get comfortable talking about your work  so many of  us have this mental hurdle of am i  bragging  is it too much should i be talking about  myself shouldn't my work be talking  about myself  but the reality is we are great  cheerleaders of others  we talk at length about their  accomplishments but and we need to be  equally good at talking about our own  work  to value your own perspective and remind  yourself often  it's super easy to get into that  comparison trap but a difference  is not a weakness if you're not happy  with the current way of working or  with the culture of our society and you  want to be the one to initiate the  change  my strategy is to set your mindset to be  curious  and optimistic and stay persistent with  what you believe  embrace changes as they come and be  prepared for any opportunities that may  come by  so that you're always ready to take on  new opportunities  do not fear be brave woman belonging  tech do not let anyone make it otherwise
 

